<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE- Hotel Prop H1 net up to S$13.3 mln.</title>
<headline>TABLE- Hotel Prop H1 net up to S$13.3 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			    13.33  vs  10.71</p>
<p>Group shr (cents)		    3.27  vs   2.64</p>
<p>    Turnover			     311.12  vs 265.62</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	4.91  vs   3.82</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  13.68  vs   9.92</p>
<p>    Depreciation and amortisation   17.39  vs  16.39</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			41.33  vs  36.43</p>
<p>    Losses from associates	     3.34  vs   1.56</p>
<p>    Tax				     18.49  vs  14.94</p>
<p>    Minorities			     6.17  vs   9.23</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			0.28  vs   1.28</p>
<p>Note - Hotel Properties Ltd said a rise in net profit was due to a higher return on its Nassim Jade condominium project and the sale of 3 condominium units at Four Seasons Park. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
